-- title:
--   Natural families into a scheme are determined on split coefficient maps
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, with $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$, and $(r) = (\pi)$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra, $\mathrm{Fr}$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for all $x$. Write $E$ for the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $Onr$ on which $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ agrees with the identity, and $E_n := E/(\pi^{n+1})$ for a given $n$. Let $Y$ assign to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ a type $Y.obj\,B$, functorially in $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms, let $T$ be a scheme, and let $F, F'$ assign to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1} = 0$ in $B$, each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $c : E_n \to B$ and each $y \in Y.obj\,B$ a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to T$, both natural in the sense that for $\varphi : B \to B'$ the value at $(\varphi \circ c, Y.map\,\varphi\,y)$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by the value at $(c,y)$. Assume $F$ and $F'$ agree at all $(c,y)$ for which $c$ composed with $E \to E_n$ is the restriction to $E$ of some $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to B$. Then $F\,B\,c\,y = F'\,B\,c\,y$ for every such $B$, every $c$ and every $y$.
--
--   This is the descent step showing that coefficient maps which extend to $Onr$ suffice to pin down a natural family of morphisms into a scheme: the fixed ring $E$ of $\mathrm{Fr}^2$ is a discrete valuation ring over which $Onr$ is faithfully flat, so $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the base change is an epimorphism. It is used in the construction of the descended quotient map on the formal model of the $p$-adic upper half plane, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_univ`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_univ).
